0..77 Comment "// The binding field in rule terms (Kaposi and Xie, _Second-Order Generalised"
78..156 Comment "// Algebraic Theories_, FSCD 2024, doi:10.4230/LIPIcs.FSCD.2024.10). At a port"
157..235 Comment "// written `pi+ (x : S) . T` a rule writes `bind x . t` for the field the port"
236..313 Comment "// binds: `x` is a variable of the representable sort `S`, which substitution"
314..385 Comment "// instantiates. At a port written `bind (a : N) . T` the same spelling"
386..465 Comment "// abstracts the atom `a` (`bind-term.gandr`), which swapping renames. The port"
466..546 Comment "// decides which: the value of `Theory` keeps a field as `Bind` and its variable"
547..626 Comment "// as `Bvar`, an abstraction as `Abs` and its atom as `Occ`, so a program tells"
627..662 Comment "// the two binders apart by `case`."
664..738 Comment "/// A receive on a restricted channel: `nu` abstracts the channel `c`, and"
739..815 Comment "/// `listen`\'s continuation is a field binding the value `x` received on it."
816..889 Comment "/// No process outside the restriction can name `c` to send on it, so the"
890..965 Comment "/// receive never fires. The checker orients the law and the kernel replays"
966..982 Comment "/// the verdict."
